(- dispatch shift_candidate_alpha (execute_schedule_dispatch) to free vehicle_unit_gamma and dispatch slot, also make dispatched shift_candidate_alpha true.)
(- allocate vehicle_unit_gamma to shift_candidate_beta (allocate_vehicle_unit))
(- attach_task_profile to origin_availability_alpha)
(- attach_task_profile to destination_availability_alpha)
(- attach_task_profile to shift_candidate_beta)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness for origin_availability_alpha)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness for destination_availability_alpha)
(- confirm_candidate_preparedness for shift_candidate_beta)
(- activate_origin_node (origin))
(- load_origin_payload (origin))
(- unload_origin_payload (origin))
(- activate_destination_node (destination))
(- load_destination_payload (destination))
(- unload_destination_payload (destination))
(- assemble_transport_leg (basic))
(- authorize_transport_leg_loading (using origin_availability_locked and candidate_task_profile_linked origin))
(- mark_origin_availability_dispatch_ready)
(- mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready)
(- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate for origin_availability_alpha (needs dispatch_ready origin, task_profile_linked origin, dispatch_slot_available))
(- execute_origin_dispatch (to dispatch origin))
(- allocate_dispatch_slot_for_candidate for destination_availability_alpha (needs dispatch_ready destination, task_profile_linked destination, dispatch_slot_available))
(- (no execute for destination))
(We also need to ensure we have candidate_task_profile_linked for origin and destination before activate and unload. We'll attach before activate.)
(Now we need to check preconditions for each action and ensure we satisfy them.)
(Let's simulate.)
(Initial state:)
(- candidate_created origin_availability_alpha: true)
(- vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha: true)
(- candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha: false)
(- cargo_available: true)
(- origin_availability_locked: false)
(- origin_availability_confirmed: false)
(- origin_node_ready: false)
(- origin_node_occupied: false)
(- origin_availability_node_linked: true)
(- candidate_prepared origin: false)
(- operator_available driver_operator_alpha: true)
(- etc.)
(Now step 1: release_compliance_certificate shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha (true). Effect: compliance_certificate_available true, not candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha.)
(After: compliance_certificate_available true, candidate_compliance_certificate_linked shift_candidate_alpha compliance_certificate_alpha false.)
(Step 2: execute_schedule_dispatch shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma dispatch_slot_alpha)
(Precondition: dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha (true), candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_alpha vehicle_unit_gamma (true), candidate_dispatch_slot_linked shift_candidate_alpha dispatch_slot_alpha (true), not dispatched shift_candidate_alpha (true). Effect: dispatched shift_candidate_alpha true, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true, dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha true. Note: dispatch_allocated remains true (not removed). So after: dispatch_allocated shift_candidate_alpha true, dispatched shift_candidate_alpha true, vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma true, dispatch_slot_available dispatch_slot_alpha true.)
(Step 3: allocate_vehicle_unit shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma)
(Precondition: candidate_created shift_candidate_beta (true), not vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta (true), vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma (true). Effect: vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta true, candidate_vehicle_linked shift_candidate_beta vehicle_unit_gamma true, not vehicle_available vehicle_unit_gamma.)
(After: vehicle_allocated shift_candidate_beta true, vehicle_unit_gamma not available.)
(Step 4: attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_created origin_availability_alpha (true), vehicle_allocated origin_availability_alpha (true), route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha (true). Effect: candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha true, not route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha.)
(After: route_task_profile_alpha becomes unavailable.)
(Step 5: attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Precondition: candidate_created destination_availability_alpha (true), vehicle_allocated destination_availability_alpha (true), route_task_profile_available route_task_profile_alpha? Wait we just made it unavailable in step 4. So we cannot attach again because route_task_profile_available is false. We need another route_task_profile? There's only one route_task_profile_alpha defined. So we cannot attach task profile to both origin and destination using same profile because after first attach, it becomes unavailable. However we might not need task profile linked for destination? Let's check requirements: activate_destination_node requires candidate_task_profile_linked destination. Unload_destination_payload requires candidate_task_profile_linked destination. So we need it. But we only have one route_task_profile_alpha. Could we reuse after releasing? There is action detach_task_profile that makes route_task_profile_available again. So we could attach to origin, then later detach, then attach to destination. However detach requires candidate_task_profile_linked ?candidate ?route_task_profile. We could detach from origin after we no longer need it? But origin needs task profile for activate_origin_node and unload_origin_payload. After we finish origin activation and unload, we might not need it further? Let's see: origin needs task profile for activate_origin_node (precondition), load_origin_payload does not need task profile, unload_origin_payload needs task profile. So we need task profile for origin up to unload_origin_payload. After unload, we might not need it further. However we also need origin_availability_locked for transport leg loading authorization (authorize_transport_leg_loading requires candidate_task_profile_linked origin_availability ?route_task_profile). So we need origin task profile linked for authorize as well. So origin needs task profile linked until after authorization. After we authorize transport leg loading, we may not need origin task profile further. However we also need origin_availability_locked etc for goal; but those are already true. So we could detach origin's task profile after authorization.)
(Similarly destination needs task profile for activate_destination_node and unload_destination_payload. After unload, we may not need it further (except maybe for dispatch_ready? mark_destination_availability_dispatch_ready does not require task profile). So we can detach after unload.)
(Thus we can attach task profile to origin, use it for origin activate, load, unload, authorize, then detach. Then attach to destination, use for destination activate, load, unload, then detach (optional). Then attach to shift_candidate_beta (need for confirm preparedness). Actually shift_candidate_beta needs task profile linked for confirm_candidate_preparedness (precondition). Also for goal we need candidate_task_profile_linked shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha. So we need to attach to shift_candidate_beta and keep it (goal requires it). So we need to keep task profile linked to shift_candidate_beta at end.)
(Thus we need to manage the single route_task_profile_alpha: we will attach to origin, use, detach; attach to destination, use, detach; attach to shift_candidate_beta and keep.)
(Thus we need detach_task_profile action.)
(Now let's outline steps with detach.)
(Step 4: attach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 5: activate_origin_node origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 6: load_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Step 7: unload_origin_payload origin_availability_alpha origin_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Step 8: detach_task_profile origin_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (makes route_task_profile_available again))
(Step 9: attach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 10: activate_destination_node destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 11: load_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Step 12: unload_destination_payload destination_availability_alpha destination_node_alpha route_task_profile_alpha cargo_payload_alpha)
(Step 13: detach_task_profile destination_availability_alpha route_task_profile_alpha (makes available again))
(Step 14: attach_task_profile shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha)
(Step 15: confirm_candidate_preparedness shift_candidate_beta route_task_profile_alpha (makes candidate_prepared shift_candidate_beta true))
(Now we have shift_candidate_beta prepared, vehicle allocated, task profile linked.)
(But we also need to prepare origin and destination via confirm_candidate_preparedness. We haven't done that yet. We need to confirm preparedness for origin and destination after attaching task profile and before activate? Actually confirm_candidate_preparedness requires candidate_task_profile_linked (true after attach) and vehicle_allocated (true). So we should do confirm after attach and before activate? Activate also requires candidate_prepared? Let's check activate_origin_node precondition: candidate_prepared ?origin_availability, candidate_task_profile_linked ?origin_availability ?route_task_profile, origin_availability_node_linked, not origin_node_ready, not origin_node_occupied. So activate requires candidate_prepared true. So we need to confirm preparedness before activate.)
(Thus order for origin: attach task profile, confirm_candidate_preparedness, activate_origin_node, load_origin_payload, unload_origin_payload, detach_task_profile.)
(Similarly for destination: attach task profile, confirm_candidate_preparedness, activate_destination_node, load_destination_payload, unload_destination_pallet, detach_task_profile.)
(Now we need to ensure we have cargo_available for loads. We'll do origin load first (cargo available), then unload (cargo available), then destination load (cargo available), then unload)
